  "details": "<p>The site is often referred to as Kh\u00f3stia, the former name of the nearby modern settlement now known as Pr\u00f3dhromos.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A complex of structures dating to the Greek and Roman period, with ceramic evidence of prior occupation of the vicinity, on a spur of Pali\u00f3vouno, overlooking a valley leading to the bay of Sar\u00e1nda on the Korinthian Gulf. The excavators associate this site with the attested classical city of Khorsiai on the basis of epigraphic evidence recovered at the site.",
